policy_response:
This is a good start! However, it does not account for case sensitivity or punctuation marks. Here's an updated implementation that handles these cases:
```
% Read texts from files
text1 = fileread('Text1.txt');
text2 = fileread('Text2.txt');
% Convert both texts to lowercase, remove punctuation, and split into words
cleanedText1 = lower(regexprep(lower(strsplit(text1)), '[^\w\s]', ''));
cleanedText2 = lower(regexprep(lower(strsplit(text2)), '[^\w\s]', ''));
% Find unique words in text1 that do not appear in text2
[~, ~, idx] = intersect(cleanedText1', cleanedText2');
uniqueWords = cleanedText1(idx);
% Print the unique words
disp(uniqueWords);
```
This implementation first removes all non-alphanumeric characters (punctuation, spaces) from both texts using regular expressions. It then splits the remaining text into individual words. Finally, it finds the intersection of the two sets of words, which gives us the unique words in `text1` that don't appear in `text2`. The resulting array is printed at the end.

